sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-asterias-rubens-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-asterias-rubens-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-asterias-rubens-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Asterias rubens Turing wavelength at 115.2 µm (Holocene, Pass 2) — MorphoEval overall 86.2/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2 keeps the square 576.0 µm Neumann patch (λ_FFT = 116.4904 µm, dispersion Pearson r = 0.999817, RMSE = 0.003533, KS = 0.0833). The pentaradial photograph, scaled onto that patch, is a negative control: std(u) falls to 0.00144 against 0.0685 on the square (ratio 0.0209), so the organism outline is not the reaction domain at 115.2 µm. Tubercle spacing is now the within-plate median (0.0168 arm-radii) against the within-plate 10th percentile (0.0100), not a transferred 5.8 mm arm. Equal-diffusion max σ remains −0.103. The GIF is 12 frames at 840×666 and ends on the Hillewaert photograph. The plate still has no scale bar. Garm & Nilsson 2014 experimented on Linckia laevigata. Overall 86.2/100 (faithfulness 85.3, reproducibility 88.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 78, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 88, Source and data traceability 91, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/asterias_rubens_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-asterias-rubens-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/png, 367344 B, 1632×984 px, artifact_sha256 1e0766613517dd66c929062b38c34dfa5e4ceca46265102ed100428ac39d9477 (sha256 1e0766613517dd66c929062b38c34dfa5e4ceca46265102ed100428ac39d9477), spec_fingerprint f1205721de3cf1a837201a21f488df08c3a58b144285920a89c856f2c63ab2f0. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: f1205721de3cf1a837201a21f488df08c3a58b144285920a89c856f2c63ab2f0; artifact_sha256: 1e0766613517dd66c929062b38c34dfa5e4ceca46265102ed100428ac39d9477; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/asterias_rubens_turing_wavelength_s0/asterias_rubens_specimen.jpg=7d7d25e638cab5b2..., datasets/asterias_rubens_turing_wavelength_s0/asterias_rubens_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=a5253b2ab52b4a62...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-asterias-rubens-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 diffusion-driven instability and a critical wavenumber. | Schnakenberg 1979 two-species reaction with a homogeneous steady state. | Murray 1981 writes the pre-pattern wavenumber used for animal markings. | Garm & Nilsson 2014: most starfish have a compound eye at the arm tip; their navigation experiments used Linckia laevigata.; reconstructed_in_script: a=0.072, b=0.918, D_v/D_u=7.62, domain 576.0 µm = 5 × 115.2 µm, seed 3123. | FTCS growth versus analytical σ(k), diffusivity sweep, equal-diffusion ablation. | Silhouette-domain quench control and a within-plate tubercle-spacing null.; transfer_boundary: The 115.2 µm length is the catalog tier, transferred onto Schnakenberg kinetics. It is not a published Asterias ocellus diameter. | The Linckia compound-eye result is not an Asterias rubens wavelength.; does_not_claim: That 115.2 µm was measured on this specimen. | That the studio photograph is a micrograph, or that its pixel scale is 115.2 µm. | That the organism silhouette is the correct 576 µm domain. The control shows it quenches the mode. | A second, independent assessor.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Resolved in this pass. Silhouette scaled onto the 576 µm patch quenches the mode (std ratio 0.0209). Production domain stays the square.', 'status': 'resolved'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Resolved in this pass. Tubercle spacing reference is the within-plate 10th percentile (0.0100 arm-radii), not an assumed 5.8 mm arm.', 'status': 'resolved'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'No independent second assessor.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'The studio photograph has no scale bar. Absolute tubercle spacing in micrometres is not claimed.'}" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.862"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, single-agent; second assessor not run)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

